e. Known to some as a Beaver Moon, November's Full Moon was also near perigee, the closest point in its elliptical orbit around planet Earth. That made it one of the biggest and brightest Full Moons, also known as a supermoon. In fact, November's Full Moon was the first in a series of four consecutive Full Moons near perigee. So your next chance to watch a supermoon rise will be when the Cold Moon rises on December 23.","img":"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Plenilunio1_2048r.jpg?w=1400&fit=clip","by":"Marcella Pace","video":false},"tle":["1 25544U 98067A   26331.13747498  .00006288  00000+0  11956-3 0  9996","2 25544  51.6313 213.6849 0007381  69.8495 290.3287 15.49629659597013"],"passes":[{"start":"2026-11-27T17:38:31Z","end":"2026-11-27T17:43:49Z","top":"2026-11-27T17:41:42Z","max":42,"from":["W","西"],"to":["SE","東南"],"mins":5},{"start":"2026-11-27T19:16:54Z","end":"2026-11-27T19:16:54Z","top":"2026-11-27T19:17:48Z","max":11,"from":["SW","西南"],"to":["SW","西南"],"mins":1},{"start":"2026-11-28T16:50:27Z","end":"2026-11-28T16:57:00Z","top":"2026-11-28T16:53:44Z","max":56,"from":["W","西"],"to":["SE","東南"],"mins":7},{"start":"2026-11-28T18:27:51Z","end":"2026-11-28T18:31:21Z","top":"2026-11-28T18:30:00Z","max":16,"from":["W","西"],"to":["S","南"],"mins":4},{"start":"2026-11-29T17:39:26Z","end":"2026-11-29T17:44:49Z","top":"2026-11-29T17:42:07Z","max":23,"from":["W","西"],"to":["S","南"],"mins":5},{"start":"2026-11-30T16:51:11Z","end":"2026-11-30T16:57:12Z","top":"2026-11-30T16:54:12Z","max":31,"from":["W","西"],"to":["SE","東南"],"mins":6},{"start":"2026-12-01T17:41:15Z","end":"2026-12-01T17:43:24Z","top":"2026-12-01T17:42:20Z","max":11,"from":["SW","西南"],"to":["SW","西南"],"mins":2},{"start":"2026-12-02T16:52:16Z","end":"2026-12-02T16:56:39Z","top":"2026-12-02T16:54:28Z","max":17,"from":["W","西"],"to":["S","南"],"mins":4}],"track":{"t0":"2026-11-27T16:27:00Z","step":60,"p":[[0.7,77.1],[-2.4,79.3],[-5.5,81.4],[-8.5,83.6],[-